# What a Raspberry Pi 5's image holds besides nova (which pulls in the
# desktop), as installer/packages is for a PC, and besides its hardware
# profile's packages (data/hardware/raspberry-pi-5/packages). One per line.
base
archlinuxarm-keyring
nova
# The Pi 5's own kernel, built from Raspberry Pi's configuration for it as
# Raspberry Pi OS's is: 16K pages, and the transparent huge pages its GPU
# driver needs for its large pages (linux-rpi is the Pi 3 and 4's, with
# neither). And the firmware that starts it, with its Wi-Fi and Bluetooth.
linux-rpi-16k
raspberrypi-bootloader
firmware-raspberrypi
linux-firmware
# Which Wi-Fi channels the country allows, set from the time zone at the
# first start (nova-first-boot).
wireless-regdb
iw
# SSH, and sudo. (git and base-devel come with nova, for nova apps install.)
openssh
sudo
# A console editor and completion, for the day the desktop does not start.
nano
bash-completion
unzip
# The Activity window (Super+Ctrl+T), and a summary of the system.
btop
fastfetch
# Screen recording, from the Capture menu.
gpu-screen-recorder
